meta {
  name: create-item
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/admin/v1/menu/items
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "category_uid": "{{category_uid}}",
    "name": "Tomato Shorba",
    "description": "Roasted tomato, black pepper",
    "price_minor": 18000,
    "food_type": "veg",
    "spice_level": "mild",
    "prep_time_mins": 12,
    "sort_order": 10
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 201 && res.body.data) {
    bru.setVar("admin_item_uid", res.body.data.uid)
  }
}

tests {
  test("responds 201, or 409 if the name is taken", function () {
    expect([201, 409]).to.include(res.status)
  })

  test("price is echoed as integer paise plus a display string", function () {
    if (res.status === 201) {
      expect(res.body.data.price.minor).to.equal(18000)
      expect(res.body.data.price.display).to.equal("₹180.00")
    }
  })
}

docs {
  # Create a menu item

`price_minor` is **paise**, as an integer: 18000 is ₹180.00. No float reaches the server
(docs/DECISIONS.md D7). The admin UI parses what a manager types and rejects more than two decimal
places rather than rounding -- a mistyped `180.555` must be a visible error, not a silently altered
price.

**`food_type` is required and has no default.** Guessing "veg" would mislabel meat; guessing
"non_veg" would hide vegetarian dishes from diners filtering for them. Omit it to see
`TX_MNU_015` (422).
}
